WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:00.850 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Collins  gift bags and Applause  This Plane full of Chinese tourists was  greeted in Thailand by cabinet ministers  and a crowd of onlookers holding  welcoming banners now we can say  Thailand is really open for all tourism  they were the first to visit the country  since China reopened its borders after  three years of heavy restrictions  before the pandemic Chinese Travelers  were the largest source of Tourism  Revenue globally spending 255 billion  dollars around the world  the travel analysts say limited flights  travel restrictions and lower demand are  slowing down the return of these big  spending International visitors at least  for now  for nearly three years strict quarantine  requirements have kept millions of  Chinese tourists from traveling abroad  travel into and out of mainland China  dropped by more than 94 to 8.8 million  trips in 2021 from 170 million in 2019.  but in January China's government  removed the restrictions that stifled  the flow of these Travelers who were  particularly important for tourism  hotspots in the U.S Europe and Southeast  Asia take Singapore for example where  visitors from mainland China made up  nearly a fifth of international arrivals  in 2019 and spent around 3.1 billion  dollars businesses in Southeast Asia  have lost an estimated 6 million tourism  jobs since 2019 and have struggled to  find alternative sources of revenue  now even as some countries begin  welcoming back Chinese tourists analysts  say the regional industry won't recover  until 2024 and maybe even longer for the  rest of the world  so why will recovery take so long  firstly flight capacity is limited when  China closed its borders to  international travel in 2020 many  airlines rerouted their fleets to serve  other destinations and now with high  Fuel and operational costs many are not  rushing to resume pre-pandemic routes to  and from China days after China reopened  its borders there were only 16  international flights scheduled to  depart from Beijing Capital  International Airport  and then there's the travel restrictions  some governments are wary about Rising  covert cases coming out of China and  have implemented travel rules in  December Italy traditionally among the  top destinations for Chinese tourists  became the first EU country to introduce  covert testing on arrival for those  coming from China many other countries  have announced similar requirements  prompting China to criticize the  measures  and lastly the demand for traveling  abroad is still low today flights in and  out of Northeast Asia the region that  includes China are still about 60 below  pre-pandemic levels and the Lunar New  Year holidays are expected to see people  mostly travel domestically as they  reunite with family that means demand  for international flights won't pick up  until the second quarter of the Year  according to analysts  the Ripple effects of this delayed  recovery and travel have wide economic  implications  sectors that are connected to tourism  like hospitality and luxury goods have  suffered while Chinese tourists stayed  home shares of some luxury goods  companies such as lvmh have rallied  since China announced the easing of  restrictions and analysts say it's just  one of the industries that have high  hopes for when Chinese Travelers start  spending again  [Music]

